From d8bcdfa1d0f1a4b0ec88d304bdb951b24bae9adf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernt Budde <bernt.budde@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:45:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/85] Tokenizer: a method name, a postfix ++/-- and a
 subscript's } end a term
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a term perl expects an operator.  _opcontext now knows the three
ends of a term its tables could not see, through one predicate,
_ends_term_at:

  * a method name: a Word right after ->  ($o->w*w() multiplies);
  * a postfix ++ or --, which is the one that itself follows a term
    ($i++ / 2 divides; the prefix ++$i still opens a term);
  * the } of a subscript or a dereference block, told from a block's }
    by the token before its matching {: a Symbol, ->, } or ] makes a
    subscript, a Cast a dereference, do or eval a value block, anything
    else a block ($h{a}%-1 is a modulo, @{$h}*$x a multiplication).

A match, a substitution, a transliteration and a here-doc join the
classes that end a term (/a/.2 concatenates).

The % and * arms of Token::Unknown, the .digit test of Token::Operator
and the / arm of Token::Whitespace ask one helper, _after_term (it keeps
the scalar filehandle slot of print $fh LIST out, as before), and
_cast_or_op's } branch uses the same brace scan, _curly_kind.  The old
scan stopped at the first ; or ( inside the block, so after
`for (1) { $h{$_}; }` it took the subscript's } for the block's opener
and made the * of a following *{"main::x"} = ... an operator; it now
counts braces only, which fixes that row too.  After a block's } the
.digit test now says number (print {$fh} .5 prints 0.5).

Regression pairs 52-54 for the three cases (the plans of 08_regression.t
and 25_increment.t enumerate the directory).  Fixes PCL §55 and §33 in
t/ppi_bugs_pcl.t; the §11 row "no typeglob symbol may be manufactured
out of the second pattern" passes as well, because the * in its
mis-lexed second pattern now follows a Regexp token (§11 itself is not
fixed: row 13 stays TODO).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
